# `XS.forEach(x => { s += x; })`, `XS.reduce((a, x) => a + x, 0)` over a list of whole numbers: the library's pair "is an own element at i in a plain vector" | "that element" gave a boxed value of which nothing was known:
# the tag was asked in every turn, the poll was read in every turn, and the turns stood one by one: fourteen instructions an element where a for-of over the same list has under five.
# The row for a plain vector of numbers (IsElementPresent | GetArrayElement by the kind of storage that is asked once in front of the loop) was bound to callees that take fractions. It is taken for whole numbers
# too, in the bodies that store nothing into a list: forEach, reduce, some, every, find, findIndex. The kind is tested in front; a list of another kind goes by the copy beside; a hole leaves the run as before.
# f1 = total . f2 = often, into whose loop total is copied
# -- source: main.cjs
